# Colleges & Programs UI — Task Plan & Implementation Log

## Plan
- High-level goal: Implement the desktop UI for the "Colleges & Programs" administration tab using DaisyUI components, adhering strictly to the user-provided layout screenshot.
- Scope:
  - Frontend only (no backend database mutations as requested).
  - Page Route: `/admin/colleges` rendered via `AdminController@colleges`.
  - Header with breadcrumbs (`Administration > Colleges & Programs`), title, description, and "+ Add Program" and "+ Add College" buttons.
  - Three summary statistic cards: "Colleges & Satellites" (17), "Degree Programs" (127), and "Accreditation Progress" with segmented progress bar and colored status legend.
  - Search and multi-criteria filter bar (Campus, College, Level).
  - Left column: "COLLEGES DIRECTORY" grouped by campus (BU Gubat, BU Guinobatan, BU Polangui, BU Tabaco, Daraga Campus, Legazpi East Campus, Main Campus, etc.) with avatar acronyms, program count badges, active states, and selection events.
  - Right column: Selected college card (avatar, name, count badge, action buttons) and "DEGREE PROGRAMS MATRIX" table with codes, titles, accreditation status badges, and action buttons.
  - Interactive DaisyUI modals for "Add Academic Degree Program" and "Add College / Satellite".
  - Follow the 150–200 line cap rule by breaking into modular sub-components and partials.
- Key decisions:
  - Use DaisyUI 5 components (`card`, `table`, `badge`, `btn`, `input`, `select`, `modal`).
  - Institutional color palette: BU Orange (`#F26522`) and BU Blue (`#0038A8` / `#1D4ED8`).
  - Store realistic mock data representing all 17 Bicol University colleges/units and their degree programs.
- Testing strategy:
  - Verify route loads via dev login (`/dev/login/sysadmin` or `/dev/login/iqa-staff`).
  - Run `npm run build` and `php artisan test` to ensure zero regressions.

